DEDICATED OUTDOOR AIR SYSTEM (DOAS): FURNISHED BY OWER

1) GENERAL
a. THE AHU CONSISTS OF ONE SUPPLY FAN WITH VFD, ONE EXHAUST FAN WITH VFD, ONE ENERGY RECOVERY WHEEL WITH VFD, ONE CHILLED WATER COIL, ONE HOT WATER PREHEAT COIL, FILTERS.

2) THE BMS CONTRACTOR SHALL
a. FURNISH, MOUNT AND WIRE ANY ADDITIONAL COMPONENTS NOT PROVIDED BY THE UNIT MANUFACTURER TO ACHI EVE A COMPLETELY OPERATIONAL SYSTEM.
b. FURNISH ONE (1) PRIMARY CONTROL PANEL.
c. PROVIDE OUTDOOR AIR, DISCHARGE AIR AND EXHAUST AIR FLOW MEASURING STATION FOR MONITORING.
d. PROVIDE ALL LABOR AND EQUIPMENT, INCLUDING WIRING, REQUIRED TO CONN ECT THE DOAS UNIT'S MANUFACTURER CONTROLS TO THE BMS VIA COMMUNICATION INTERFACE. THE BMS SHALL MONITOR ALL POINTS AVAILABLE VIA THE INTERFACE. COORDINATE WITH THE MANUFACTURER.

3) SAFETIES
a. THE SUPPLY AND/OR RETURN SMOKE DETECTOR SHALL STOP THE SUPPLY AND RETURN/EXHAUST FANS UPON THE PRESENCE OF SMOKE THROUGH THE FAS.
b. A HIGH DISCHARGE AIR PRESSURE SWITCH LOCATED DOWNSTREAM OF THE SUPPLY FAN AND UPSTREAM OF THE CLOSEST DAMPER SHALL STOP THE SUPPLY AND RETURN/EXHAUST FANS WHEN DUCT PRESSURE EXCEEDS DESIGN.
c. A LOW SUCTION AIR PRESSURE SWITCH LOCATED UPSTREAM OF THE RETURN/EXHAUST FAN AND DOWNSTREAM OF THE CLOSEST DAMPER SHALL STOP THE SUPPLY AND RETURN/EXHAUST FANS WHEN DUCT PRESSURE DECREASES BELOW DESIGN.
d. FREEZESTATS INSTALLED ON THE INLET OF THE COOLING COIL SHALL DISABLE TlHE UNIT UPON SENSING A TEMPERATURE BELOW 38'F (ADJ.) FOR A PERIOD OF 1 80 SECONDS (ADJ). ONCE THE FREEZESTAT HAS BEEN ACTIVATED, MANUAL RESET A TTHE BMS PANEL SHALL BE REQUIRED TO ALLOW THE SYSTEM TO RESTART. THE STEAM/HOT WATER VALVE SHALL MODULATE AS NECESSARY TO MA INTAIN A PREHEAT COIL DISCHARGE AIR TEMPERATURE OF 90° F (ADJ.).
e. A LEAK DETECTOR LOCATED IN THE DRAIN PAN BELOW THE UNIT SHALL SOUND AN ALARM AT THE BMS UPON SENSING WATER.

4) WARM-UP / COOL_DOWN
a. WARM-UP (heating season): INVOKED IF RETURN AIR TEMP < 60° F (ADJ.) AT STARTUP. RESET SUPPLY AIR TEMP TO 80° F (ADJ.) AND OPEN ALL DOWNSTREAM VAV BOXES TO MAXIMUM CFM. RESET SUPPLY AIR TEMP LINEARLY AND INVERSELY FROM 80° F (ADJ) TO 70° F (ADJ.) AS RETURN AIR TEMP INCREASES FROM 60° F (ADJ.) TO 70° F (ADJ.). DURING WARM-UP, AIR HANDLING UNIT SHALL OPERATE ON 100% RETURN AIR. AFTER WARM-UP (RETURN AIR ABOVE 70° F (ADJ.)), UNIT SHALL BE CONTROLLED AS DESCRIBED IN OCCUPIED MODE.
b. COOL_DOWN (cooling season): INVOKED IF RETURN AIR TEMP > 80° F (ADJ.) AT STARTUP. RESET SUPPLY AIR TEMP TO 55° F (ADJ.) AND OPEN ALL VAV BOXES TO MAXIMUM CFM. DURING COOL_DOWN, AIR HANDLING UNIT SHALL OPERATE ON 100% RETURN AIR. AFTER COOL_DOWN (RETURN AIR BELOW 70'F (ADJ.)), UNIT SHALL BE CONTROLLED AS DESCRIBED IN OCCUPIED MODE.

5) OCCUPIED MODE
a. START: AHU SHALL BE STARTED BASED ON A START TIME OPTIMIZATION PROGRAM, TIME OF DAY SCHEDULE OR MANUAL COMMAND AND RUN CONTINUOUSLY.
b. ENABLE VAV BOXES PRIOR TO SUPPLY FAN START.
c. UPON START COMMAND: ALL ASSOCIATED ISOLATION DAMPERS AND FIRE/SMOKE DAMPERS LOCATED AT THE UNIT SHALL OPEN. ISOLATION DAMPERS AND FIRE/SMOKE DAMPERS SHALL BE HARDWIRE INTERLOCKED TO THE SUPPLY FAN STARTER BY THE BMS CONTRACTOR. THE OUTSIDE AIR, EXHAUST AIR AND RETURN AIR DAMPERS SHALL MODULATE TO MINIMUM POSITION. HARDWIRED DAMPER END SWITCHES ON ALL 2-POSITION DAMPERS SHALL ENERGIZE THE SUPPLY AND RETURN/EXHAUST FAN STARTERS WHEN ALL ASSOCIATED DAMPERS ARE IN THEIR FULLY OPEN POSITION.
d. FANS AND CONTROLS: SUPPLY AND EXHAUST FAN VFDs SHALL START UNLOADED AND SLOWLY RAMP UP. IN OCCUPIED MODE, SUPPLY AND EXHAUST FANS RUN CONTINUOUSLY. SUPPLY FAN VFD SHALL BE CONTROLLED TO MAINTAIN SUPPLY STATIC PRESSURE SETPOINT, SENSED AT A POINT 2/3 DOWNSTREAM OF THE SUPPLY FAN. EXHAUST FAN VFD SHALL BE CONTROLLED TO MAINTAIN EXHAUST CFM, AS SENSED BY AN EXHAUST AIRFLOW MEASURING STATION, AT THE EXHAUST CFM SETPOINT. THE EXHAUST CFM SETPOINT SHALL BE CALCULATED BY DEDUCT A FIXED VALUE (ADJ) TO THE SUPPLY CFM, AS SENSED BY A SUPPLY AIRFLOW MEASURING STATION.

6) ECONOMIZER MODE
a. ECONOMIZER AVAILABLE WHEN OUTSIDE AIR ENTHALPY < ENERGY RECOVERY UNIT RETURN AIR ENTHALPY AND OUTSIDE AIR DRY BULB < 65° F (ADJ.). WHEN IN COOLING MODE AND ECONOMIZER IS AVAILABLE:
    - IF RISE IN SUPPLY AIR TEMP ABOVE SETPOINT: OUTSIDE AIR DAMPER SHALL REMAIN OPEN, ENERGY RECOVERY COIL BYPASS DAMPERS SHALL OPEN, ENERGY RECOVERY COIL VFD SHALL RAMP DOWN.
    - UPON FURTHER RISE ABOVE SETPOINT: OUTSIDE AIR DAMPER REMAINS OPEN, ENERGY RECOVERY COIL BYPASS DAMPER SHALL MODULATE CLOSED; ERU SHALL OPERATE IN ENERGY RECOVERY MODE.
    - UPON FURTHER RISE: OUTSIDE AIR DAMPER REMAINS OPEN, BYPASS DAMPERS CLOSED, CHILLED WATER COIL VALVE SHALL STAGE ON AS NECESSARY TO MAINTAIN SETPOINT.
    - IF SUPPLY AIR TEMP DROPS BELOW SETPOINT: CHILLED WATER VALVE SHALL CLOSE. IF CHILLED WATER VALVE IS CLOSED AND SUPPLY AIR TEMP CONTINUES TO DROP BELOW SETPOINT: RECOVERY COIL BYPASS DAMPERS SHALL BE CLOSED AND OPERATE IN ENERGY RECOVERY MODE.
b. WHEN ECONOMIZER NOT AVAILABLE: HEAT RECOVERY COIL AND CHILLED WATER VALVE SHALL OPERATE IN SEQUENCE AS NECESSARY TO MAINTAIN SUPPLY AIR TEMPERATURE SETPOINT.

7) ENERGY RECOVERY MODE
a. ENERGY RECOVERY WHEEL SHALL BE FIRST STAGE OF COOLING OR HEATING. IN ENERGY RECOVERY MODE, ENERGY RECOVERY COIL BYPASS DAMPERS SHALL REMAIN CLOSED. ENERGY RECOVERY WHEEL VFD SHALL MODULATE FROM MINIMUM TO MAXIMUM SPEED AS NECESSARY TO MAINTAIN DISCHARGE AIR TEMPERATURE SETPOINT(S).
b. WHEN UNIT IS NOT OPERATING IN ENERGY RECOVERY, THE CHILLED WATER VALVE AND HOT WATER HEATING COIL MODULATE/STAGE IN SEQUENCE TO MAINTAIN THE DISCHARGE AIR TEMPERATURE SETPOINT.

8) COOLING RECOVERY MODE
a. WHEN RETURN AIR ENTHALPY IS GREATER THAN OUTSIDE AIR ENTHALPY PLUS A DIFFERENTIAL (2° F (ADJ.)), THE ENERGY RECOVER COIL SHALL BE ENABLED. THE ENERGY RECOVERY WHEEL SHALL START. THE ENERGY RECOVERY UNIT SHALL MAINTAIN A DISCHARGE AIR TEMPERATURE SETPOINT OF 2°F (ADJ.) GREATER THAN THE UNIT DISCHARGE AIR TEMPERATURE SETPOINT.

9) HEATING RECOVERY MODE
a. WHEN RETURN AIR ENTHALPY IS GREATER THAN OUTSIDE AIR ENTHALPY PLUS A DIFFERENTIAL (2° F (ADJ.)), THE ENERGY RECOVER UNIT SHALL BE ENABLED. THE ENERGY RECOVERY WHEEL SHALL START. THE ENERGY RECOVERY UNIT SHALL MAINTAIN A DISCHARGE AIR TEMPERATURE SETPOINT OF 2°F (ADJ.) GREATER THAN THE UNIT DISCHARGE AIR TEMPERATURE SETPOINT.

10) COOLING MODE
a. DURING COOLING MODE, THE CHILLED WATER VALVES SHALL MODULATE AS NECESSARY TO MAINTAIN THE COOLING SETPOINT OF 74'F (ADJ.). WHEN THE DISCHARGE AIR TEMPERATURE DROPS BELOW THE COOLING SETPOINT PLUS A DEAD BAND, THE CHILLLED WATER VALVE SHALL OFF.

11) HEATING MODE
a. HEATING MODE SHALL BE ENABLED WHEN THE DISCHARGE AIR TEMPERATURE DROPS BELOW THE HEATING RECOVERY COIL DISCHARGE TEMPERATURE SETPOINT FOR AN ADJUSTABLE TIME DELAY. HEATING MODE SHALL BE DISABLED WHEN THE DISCHARGE AIR TEMPERATURE RISES ABOVE THE HEATING SETPOINT PLUS A DEADBAND.
b. DURING HEATING MODE, THE PREHEAT COIL VALVE SHALL MODULATE AS NECESSARY TO MAINTAIN THE DISCHARGE TEMPERATURE SETPOINT (ADJ.). WHEN THE DISCHARGE AIR TEMPERATURE RISES ABOVE THE HEATING SETPOINT PLUS A DEADBAND, THE PREHEAT COIL VALVE SHALL MODULATE CLOSE TO MAINTAIN SETPOINT.

12) FROST PROTECTION
a. THE ENERGY RECOVERY UNIT SHALL RUN FOR 10 SEC (ADJ.) EVERY 30 MINS (ADJ.) WHENEVER THE OUTSIDE AIR TEMPERATURE DROPS BELOW THE HEAT WHEEL DEFROST SETPOINT. DURING FROST PROTECTION MODE, THE ENERGY RECOVERY WHEEL SHALL STOP.
b. WHEN THE UNIT IS NOT OPERATING IN ENERGY RECOVERY, THE CHILLED WATER VALVE AND HEATING COIL MODULATE/STAGE IN SEQUENCE TO MAINTAIN THE DISCHARGE AIR TEMPERATURE SETPOINT.
c. ECONOMIZER MODE SHALL BE AVAILABLE WHENEVER THE OUTSIDE AIR ENTHALPY IS LESS THAN THE AIR HANDLING UNIT RETURN AIR ENTHALPY. IF ECONOMIZER IS AVAILABLE AND THERE IS A RISE IN SUPPLY AIR TEMPERATURE ABOVE THE SUPPLY AIR TEMPERATURE SETPOINT:
    - OUTSIDE AIR DAMPERS AND EXHAUST AIR DAMPERS SHALL BE MODULATED OPEN FROM MINIMUM POSITION TO 100% OPEN AS NECESSARY TO MAINTAIN THE SUPPLY AIR TEMPERATURE SETPOINT.
    - RETURN AIR DAMPERS SHALL MODULATE CLOSED PROPORTIONATELY AS THE OUTSIDE AIR AND EXHAUST AIR DAMPERS MODULATE OPEN.
    - IF OUTSIDE AIR DAMPER IS 100% OPEN AND FURTHER RISE OCCURS: OUTSIDE AIR DAMPER SHALL REMAIN 100% OPEN AND THE CHILLED WATER VALVE SHALL MODULATE OPEN AS NECESSARY TO MAINTAIN SUPPLY AIR TEMPERATURE SETPOINT.
d. WHEN ECONOMIZER MODE IS NOT AVAILABLE, THE CHILLED WATER VALVE AND STEAM/HOT WATER VALVE SHALL MODULATE IN SEQUENCE AS NECESSARY TO MAINTAIN THE SUPPLY AIR TEMPERATURE SETPOINT. THE STEAM/HOT WATER VALVE SHALL MODULATE AS NECESSARY TO MAINTAIN A MINIMUM PREHEAT COIL DISCHARGE AIR TEMPERATURE SETPOINT OF 45'F (ADJ.).
e. IF THE RETURN AIR HUMIDITY RISES ABOVE THE DEHUMIDIFICATION SETPOINT OF 60% RH (ADJ.), THE CHILLED WATER VALVE SHALL BE OVERRIDDEN OPEN AS NECESSARY TO MAINTAIN THE RETURN AIR HUMIDITY SETPOINT OF 50% (ADJ.).
f. THE OUTSIDE AIR, RETURN AIR, AND EXHAUST AIR DAMPERS SHALL BE OVERRIDDEN AS NECESSARY TO MAINTAIN THE MIXED AIR LOW LIMIT SETPOINT.
g. THE OUTSIDE AIR AND EXHAUST AIR DAMPERS SHALL BE OVERRIDDEN OPEN AS NECESSARY TO MAINTAIN THE RETURN AIR OR SPACE CARBON DIOXIDE LEVEL AT THE SETPOINT. THE CARBON DIOXIDE LEVEL SETPOINT SHALL BE EQUAL TO 700 PPM (ADJ.). THE RETURN AIR DAMPER SHALL MODULATE CLOSED PROPORTIONATELY AS THE OUTSIDE AIR AND EXHAUST AIR DAMPERS MODULATE OPEN.
h. THE SUPPLY STATIC PRESSURE SETPOINT SHALL BE RESET BASED ON VAV BOX DAMPER POSITION. IF NO VAV BOX IS GREATER THAN 85% (ADJ.) OPEN, DECREASE THE SUPPLY AIR STATIC PRESSURE UNTIL AT LEAST ONE (1) VAV BOX IS GREATER THAN 85% (ADJ.) OPEN. IF A VAV BOX IS GREATER THAN 95% (ADJ.) OPEN, INCREASE THE STATIC PRESSURE SETPOINT UNTIL THE VAV BOX IS BELOW 95% (ADJ.) OPEN.
i. THE SUPPLY TEMPERATURE SETPOINT SHALL BE RESET BASED ON VAV CFM. EVERY 15 MINUTES EACH VAV BOX SHALL BE POLLED. IF ANY VAV BOX IS PROVIDING MAXIMUM CFM, LOWER SUPPLY AIR TEMPERATURE BY 0.25° F. IF NO VAV BOX IS PROVIDING GREATER THAN 75% (ADJ.) OF MAXIMUM CFM, INCREASE THE SUPPLY AIR TEMPERATURE BY 0.25° F. IF NEITHER CONDITION EXISTS, SUPPLY TEMPERATURE SETPOINT SHALL REMAIN UNCHANGED. THIS PROGRAM SHALL BE ACTIVATED 1 HOUR AFTER OCCUPANCY START TIME.

13) UNOCCUPIED MODE
a. THE SUPPLY AND RETURN/EXHAUST FANS SHALL REMAIN OFF AND THE VFDs SHALL BE SET TO 0%. THE RETURN AIR DAMPER SHALL OPEN AND THE OUTSIDE AIR AND EXHAUST AIR DAMPERS SHALL CLOSE. ALL ISOLATION AND FIRE/SMOKE DAMPERS SHALL CLOSE. THE CHILLED WATER VALVE SHALL CLOSE AND THE STEAM/HOT WATER VALVE SHALL MODULATE AS NECESSARY TO MAINTAIN A PREHEAT COIL DISCHARGE AIR TEMPERATURE OF 45° F (ADJ.). THE HUMIDIFIER CONTROL VALVE SHALL REMAIN CLOSED.
b. IF THE RETURN AIR TEMPERATURE OR ANY SPACE TEMPERATURE FALLS BELOW 60° F (ADJ.), THE UNIT SHALL RUN AS PER WARM-UP MODE UNTIL THE RETURN AIR TEMPERATURE OR SPACE TEMPERATURE EXCEEDS 64° F (ADJ.). THE UNIT SHALL RUN A MINIMUM OF 1/2 HOUR (ADJ.) AFTER START UP.
c. IF THE RETURN AIR TEMPERATURE OR ANY SPACE TEMPERATURE RISES ABOVE 80° F (ADJ.), THE UNIT SHALL RUN AS PER COOL-DOWN MODE UNTIL THE RETURN AIR TEMPERATURE OR SPACE TEMPERATURE FALLS BELOW 76° F (ADJ.). THE UNIT SHALL RUN A MINIMUM OF 1/2 HOUR (ADJ.) AFTER START UP.
